      "writtenOn": "2023-09-11T13:55:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can use cfg!(remote_attestation) macro. Unlike the [#cfg(...)] attribute, the macro doesn\u0027t remove the code if the feature is disabled.\n\nAlternatively, I think you can add #[cfg(request_certificate)] to the `use crate::rkpvm::request_certificate` statement, e.g.:\n\n```\n#[cfg(request_certificate)]\nuse crate::rkpvm::request_certificate;\n```",
